# Pinned bytes for the market-shear study. Fetched from their publishers, never committed:
# 1,240,632,399 bytes is too much to carry in a wiki, and it is public.
#
# TWO HONEST NOTES ON THESE DIGESTS.
#
# 1. For NASDAQ ITCH there are NO PUBLISHER DIGESTS. The listing advertises a .md5sum sidecar
#    beside every archive and a GET returns HTTP 404, re-measured for the pinned files. Both
#    ITCH digests below are OURS. They prove two readers hold the same bytes; they do not
#    prove those bytes are what the publisher meant to serve, and nothing here claims they do.
#
# 2. A JSON-RPC response is NOT BYTE-CANONICAL ACROSS PROVIDERS. Some emit a non-consensus
#    blockTimestamp per transaction and some do not — a 3,360-byte difference on block
#    14,000,000 with block hash, ordering and every transaction hash identical. The eth/*
#    digests are over the STORED FORM from the named endpoint. Digest the consensus content
#    and two honest archives agree exactly; digest the response bytes and they read as a
#    divergence that is not there.
#
# format: <sha256>  <bytes>  <path under the corpus directory>
